<title>USA: Rexel Inc Q3 shr rises.</title>
<headline>Rexel Inc Q3 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>CORAL GABLES, Fla. 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr primary		$0.29		    $0.17</p>
<p> Shr diluted		 0.29		     0.16</p>
<p> Net			  7,522		    4,165</p>
<p> Sales		    297,375		  282,263</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary	25,958		   25,200</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted	25,958		   27,812</p>
<p>	  9  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr primary		$0.80		    $0.55</p>
<p> Shr diluted		 0.80		     0.50</p>
<p> Net			 20,699		   13,337</p>
<p> Sales		    854,023		  849,777</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary	25,986		   24,567</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted	25,986		   28,921</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE - In the 1995 Q3, the company reported an extraordinary, after-tax charge of $1.5 million, or $0.06 per share, related to the redemption of its then-outstanding seven percent convertible subordinated debentures due 2014.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
